course: dictionary
lesson: 1797
title: Close: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» Here close means shut, so the gate must be pushed until it is not open.
explain: Close can also mean near, and then it is said «klohs». «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer» means he sits nearer and nearer to the board. The spelling is the same, so read the clues before you decide.
explain: Close can also describe something. «Close friends» are very good friends, and «a close game» is one where the scores are nearly the same. Ask yourself whether the meaning is shut, near or describing. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Close (verb) means to shut, or to stop being open.
fact: Close (said «klohs») means near, as in «close by».
fact: Close friends are very good friends.
fact: A close game is one where the scores are nearly the same.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is right.
exercise: «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» What does close mean here? | Near | *Shut | Friendly | Quiet
exercise: «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer or moving away.» Find and copy one word that means nearer. | flash | seconds | storm | *closer
exercise: Rounding 48 to the nearest ten gives 50, so 48 is «close to» 50. What does close to mean here? | Exactly the same as | Miles away from | *About, nearly | Bigger than
test: «Close friends» are very good friends. What does close mean in «close friends»? | Shut tightly | Closing time | *Very good | Far away
test: «A close game is one where the scores are nearly the same.» Which game is a close game? | A game played outside | A game with no winner | *A game where the scores are nearly equal | A game that has been shut down
exam: «If a strange dog runs at you, stand still and fold your arms in close.» In «fold your arms in close», what does close mean? | *Near to your body | Quickly | Far away | Shut tight
